The conversation focused on the PANACEA project, detailing its organization into six complementary Work Packages (WP). James requested a polished version of the project description, emphasizing clarity and confidence in the text. The discussion outlined WP1's objectives for stakeholder engagement, which includes forming advisory groups and conducting workshops to incorporate stakeholder views. WP2's policy objectives aim to connect global climate impacts with economic growth, utilizing trade models and econometric analyses to project potential losses. Key methods involve identifying best practices in GDP growth literature, applying Lasso methods to estimate trade spillovers, and analyzing the implications of climate shocks on GDP. Overall, the conversation aimed to enhance the readability and effectiveness of the project documentation.
